eferee","id":"24"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"McDavid posts 10th assist as Oilers beat Sharks 3-1 for 4th straight win","description":"— Connor McDavid recorded his 13th point of the season and 10th assist as the Edmonton Oilers beat the San Jose Sharks 3-1 on Saturday for their fourth straight win.","story":"SAN JOSE, Calif. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3895074/connor-mcdavid\">Connor McDavid</a> recorded his 13th point of the season and 10th assist as the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/edm/edmonton-oilers\">Edmonton Oilers</a> beat the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/sj/san-jose-sharks\">San Jose Sharks</a> 3-1 on Saturday for their fourth straight win.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4565231/vasily-podkolzin\">Vasily Podkolzin</a> scored his fifth goal while <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2558631/mattias-ekholm\">Mattias Ekholm</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4233882/alex-formenton\">Alex Formenton</a> also scored for Edmonton. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3042020/tristan-jarry\">Tristan Jarry</a> stopped 19 shots.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5206628/macklin-celebrini\">Macklin Celebrini</a> returned to the lineup for San Jose after missing two games with a lower-body injury. The Sharks captain scored his first goal of the season midway through the third period.\n\n\r\n              Ekholm opened the scoring at 12:37 of the first period. Podkolzin extended Edmonton’s lead 3:13 into the third, with McDavid recording the assist. He moved ahead of <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3648002/jack-eichel\">Jack Eichel</a> for the league lead in points and assists.\n\n\r\n              Formenton made it 3-0 on a backhand shot about two minutes later.\n\n\r\n              Celebrini got San Jose on the board midway through the third period, but the Sharks could not complete the comeback.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697394/yaroslav-askarov\">Yaroslav Askarov</a> made 17 saves for San Jose.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Oilers: Visit Los Angeles on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              Sharks: Host Boston on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-10T22:51:27Z"}}